{
  "id": "invert-binary-tree",
  "title": "Invert Binary Tree",
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "categories": ["tree", "dfs"],
  "descriptionMd": "Given the `root` of a binary tree, produce its **mirror image**: at every node, the left and right subtrees trade places. Return the root of the mirrored tree.\n\n**Example 1**\n\n```\nroot = [4, 2, 7, 1, 3, 6, 9]\n→ [4, 7, 2, 9, 6, 3, 1]\n```\n\n**Example 2**\n\n```\nroot = [2, 1, 3]\n→ [2, 3, 1]\n```\n\n**Example 3**\n\n```\nroot = []\n→ []\n```",
  "constraints": ["0 ≤ number of nodes ≤ 100", "-100 ≤ Node.val ≤ 100"],
  "hints": ["Swapping the two children of the root is a good start — what still needs to happen inside each child?"],
  "signature": {
    "functionName": "invertTree",
    "params": [{ "name": "root", "type": "TreeNode" }],
    "returns": "TreeNode"
  },
  "comparator": "exact",
